<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<!--
  Entitlements for the SCREENSHOT build only. Never shipped: the Mac App Store
  artifact uses BirdoVPN-macOS.entitlements.

  Why this file exists. The screenshot run signs ad-hoc, because the real
  entitlements demand a provisioning profile and a distribution-signed app
  cannot be driven by XCUITest (distribution profiles set get-task-allow=false,
  which blocks the test runner from attaching). But stripping the entitlements
  entirely broke sign-in: KeychainService writes with kSecAttrAccessGroup and
  kSecUseDataProtectionKeychain, and the data-protection keychain refuses an app
  that carries no application-identifier — the run stopped on "Could not
  securely store your session. Please try again."

  So this carries the two keys the keychain actually checks, and nothing else.
  Ad-hoc signing applies entitlements without validating them against a profile,
  which is what makes this possible at all.

  Deliberately ABSENT, and each one matters:

    * com.apple.application-identifier — carrying it made the app UNLAUNCHABLE:
      "Could not launch BirdoVPN. Runningboard has returned error 5 ... Launchd
      job spawn failed". launchd cannot validate a team-prefixed identifier
      against an ad-hoc signature, which has no team. It is not needed either:
      the keychain derives an app's access groups from keychain-access-groups
      when that is present, and only falls back to application-identifier when
      it is not.

    * com.apple.security.app-sandbox — a sandboxed ad-hoc build gets a
      different container and would not see the session it just wrote.

    * com.apple.developer.networking.networkextension — needs a real profile;
      the packet tunnel cannot load in a screenshot build regardless.

  The team prefix is written out rather than using $(AppIdentifierPrefix),
  which resolves from the provisioning profile that this build does not have.
-->
<dict>
    <key>keychain-access-groups</key>
    <array>
        <string>KPUFGR98A5.app.birdo.vpn</string>
    </array>
</dict>
</plist>
